    "basis": "A volatile write to one PROT_READ page must fault exactly once with SIGSEGV/SEGV_ACCERR and exact byte address, preserving old byte. Same byte must become writable after PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE restore. siglongjmp(savemask1) must restore active mask; original action/mask and mapping are restored/removed explicitly."
  },
  "protocol": [
    "Map one page PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE, volatile byte at page+37 write/read0x31.",
    "Record original full signal mask; install SA_SIGINFO handler, unblock SIGSEGV; PROT_READ mprotect and read confirm.",
    "sigsetjmp(recovery,1) in valid controlling expression; arm sig_atomic flag then actual volatile byte write0x52. Missing fault is fatal.",
    "Handler accepts only armed first SIGSEGV with nonnull siginfo, SEGV_ACCERR and si_addr exactly page+37. Lock-free atomic pointer target plus sig_atomic flags; only siglongjmp or _Exit120, no stdio/allocation/locks.",
    "After jump require exactly one fault/ACCERR/address, active full mask restored and SIGSEGV unblocked; denied write leaves old byte0x31.",
    "mprotect READ|WRITE, write/read0x73; checked restore original disposition and full mask, verify original logical mask members, checked munmap.",
    "Automatic variables used after jump were initialized before save and not modified between save/jump. Caller fatal paths _Exit entire process; no handler recovery for unrelated or repeated fault."
  ],
